# Southwest

## Docker Environment

Code is edited on Windows (`c:\Users\edwin\Dockers\southwest\apps\southwest`) but the app runs inside the Docker container `southwest-web-1`. Files sync automatically via bind mount — no need to copy files.

All `bench` commands must run inside the container:
```bash
docker exec -it southwest-web-1 bash -c "cd ~/frappe-bench && <command>"
```

---

## Rule 1 — DO NOT TOUCH THE CORE

All new DocTypes, scripts, pages, hooks, and configuration must live entirely inside the `southwest` custom app. Never modify Frappe or ERPNext source code directly.

If a behavior needs to change in a base doctype, use Custom Fields, Property Setters, `doc_events`, `override_doctype_class`, or `doctype_js` hooks — never edit base app files.

---

## Rule 2 — ALL CODE AND DOCUMENTATION IN ENGLISH

Every file name, variable, function, component, UI label, error message, comment, and documentation entry must be strictly in English. Zero Spanish in code.

Applies to everything: Python, JS, JSON field labels, HTML, Jinja templates, commit messages, and DEVELOPMENT.md entries. Only exception: user-facing UI strings the business explicitly requires in Spanish (e.g. customer-facing print formats) — and even then, code identifiers stay in English.

---

## Rule 3 — ALWAYS UPDATE DEVELOPMENT.MD WITH EVERY CHANGE

After every task:
1. Update the relevant section of `.docs/development.md` (Project Structure, DocType tables, Field Detail, Hooks, etc.) to reflect the new state.
2. Add a Changelog entry at the bottom: format `### YYYY-MM-DD` with bullet points per change.
3. Update the `Last Change:` timestamp at the very end of the file.

Do not close a task without updating `.docs/development.md`.
